  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Different A.P.&#39;s are constructed with the first term <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math>, the last term <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>199</mn></math>, And integral common differences. The sum of the common differences of all such, A.P&#39;s having at least&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> terms and at most&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>33</mn></math> terms is.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "53",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>st</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;term of the A.P<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>And the last term&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>199</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></math></p><p>Let the three&nbsp;term&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>&nbsp;number of terms</p><p>Now checking for what value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;we have integral common difference,</p><p>For,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>199</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>99</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8713;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></p><p>For,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>99</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>I</mi></math></p><p>.</p><p>.</p><p>.</p><p>For,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>99</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>I</mi></math></p><p>For,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>99</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>I</mi></math></p><p>So, sum of all common difference that are integer will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8721;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>53</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
